<title>BELGIUM: EU welcomes Clinton Helms-Burton move.</title>
<headline>EU welcomes Clinton Helms-Burton move.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commisison on Thursday welcomed U.S. President Bill Clinton's decision to waive for another six months parts of a law that toughens the U.S. embargo against Cuba, but reiterated its objections to the legislation.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission remains firmly opposed, as a matter of law and policy, to the imposition of extraterritorial legislaton of this kind,&quot; Trade Commissioner Sir Leon Brittan said in a statement.</p>
<p>Clinton cited the cooperation of U.S. allies in seeking to end Communist rule on the island as his reason for waiving part of the Helms-Burton law that allows U.S. citizens to sue foreign firms deemed to have profited from property confiscated from them by Cuba after the 1959 revolution led by Fidel Castro.</p>
<p>- Brussels newsroom: +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
